    <string name="dom_open">Take a seat</string>
    <string name="dom_rules">Double-six tiles. Default: two players draw seven each and draw until they can play; three players remove only double-blank (0–0), deal nine each, and never draw; four players deal seven each, individually or in opposite-seat teams (1 + 3, 2 + 4). Draw always deals seven and uses the ordered stock. Block deals seven with no drawing. The highest dealt double opens; the hand winner leads next. Match either end; doubles do not branch. Pass only when unable to play or draw. Going out scores opponents’ pips, excluding your partner. When blocked, the lowest side scores opponents’ pips minus its own; a lowest tie scores nobody. Targets: 51, 101, 151. In 151 mode, reaching 101 against all-zero opponents wins immediately. After 64 hands, the highest side wins.</string>
